Execution mode and go-qrl
-------------------------

This part of the NOTICE ships with the remotesigner binary only. The
remotesigner-consensus binary does not link the software below.

The remotesigner binary links the go-qrl library
(https://github.com/theQRL/go-qrl), licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version. Its
execution mode encodes and signs transactions with go-qrl's library
packages, which it uses unmodified; no go-qrl command (cmd/, licensed under
the GNU General Public License) is part of it. The binary is a Combined
Work in the sense of the LGPL: go-remotesigner's own code stays under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, and go-qrl stays under the LGPL. The texts of
the LGPL and of the GNU General Public License it supplements are
LICENSES/LGPL-3.0-or-later.txt and LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.

The corresponding source of each release is published with it as
remotesigner-<version>-src-vendored.tar.gz: the go-remotesigner source with
every module it links, go-qrl included, in vendor/, so that the binary can
be rebuilt with a modified go-qrl. go-qrl's own source is also at
https://github.com/theQRL/go-qrl, at the version recorded in go.mod.
Nothing in go-remotesigner's licence forbids modifying go-qrl in a
rebuilt binary or reverse engineering it to debug such modifications.


